<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>A({4},\,{1},\,{-1})</m>, <m>B({2},\,{3},\,{-5})</m> and <m>C({6},\,{-1},\,{3})</m>.</p><div>(a) <m>\overrightarrow{AB} =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/>  </div><div>(b) <m>\overrightarrow{BC} =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="ans2"/>  </div><p>(c) Choose the correct statement.</p><div><ol marker="(1)">
<li>You cannot tell without drawing the points accurately.</li>
<li>A, B and C are collinear: BC is a multiple of AB and they share the point B.</li>
<li>A, B and C are not collinear: BC is not a multiple of AB.</li>
</ol>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) <m>\overrightarrow{AB} = \mathbf{b} - \mathbf{a} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -2 \\ 2 \\ -4 \end{array}\right)}</m>. (b) <m>\overrightarrow{BC} = \mathbf{c} - \mathbf{b} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 4 \\ -4 \\ 8 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p><p>(c) Divide each component of <m>\overrightarrow{BC}</m> by the matching component of <m>\overrightarrow{AB}</m>: <m>{-2}</m>, <m>{-2}</m>, <m>{-2}</m>. They are all <m>{-2}</m>, so <m>\overrightarrow{BC} = {-2}\,\overrightarrow{AB}</m>. The vectors are parallel and share the point B, so A, B and C are collinear.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} -2 \\ 2 \\ -4 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} 4 \\ -4 \\ 8 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>(2)</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>